1
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:06,950
七万年前，他们只是地球上不起眼的一群动物。
Seventy thousand years ago, they were just an insignificant group of animals on Earth.

2
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:10,830
没有锋利的爪牙，没有强壮的身体。
No sharp claws or fangs, no powerful bodies.

3
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:16,310
但他们拥有一种力量——创造不存在的世界。
But they had one power: to create worlds that do not exist.

4
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:31,750
大约七万年前，智人的大脑里发生了一场无声的革命。
About 70,000 years ago, a silent revolution took place in the minds of Homo sapiens.

5
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:36,650
靠着闲谈“八卦”，一个部落能凝聚约一百五十人。
Through gossip, a tribe could hold together about 150 people.

6
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:42,850
更神奇的是，他们能谈论不存在的事物——神灵、祖先与传说。
Even more remarkably, they could talk about things that do not exist: gods, ancestors and legends.

7
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:49,460
你无法说服猴子交出香蕉，哪怕许诺它死后有吃不完的香蕉。
You could never convince a monkey to give you a banana by promising it unlimited bananas after death.

8
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:56,550
只有智人会相信。共同的故事，让数万人能够共同合作。
Only Sapiens believe such things. Shared stories let tens of thousands work together.

9
00:00:56,650 --> 00:01:03,170
从非洲出发，他们走遍了整个世界；所到之处，大型动物纷纷灭绝。
Out of Africa, they spread across the whole world, and wherever they went, large animals vanished.

10
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:09,790
神话、国家、文明，都诞生于人类共同相信的想象。
Myths, nations, civilizations: all were born from imagination that humans share.

11
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:20,050
约一万两千年前，人类驯服了植物。
About 12,000 years ago, humans tamed plants.

12
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:24,610
我们以为驯化了小麦，其实是小麦驯化了我们。
We thought we domesticated wheat. In fact, wheat domesticated us.

13
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:31,050
农民更辛苦，吃得更差——赫拉利称之为“史上最大的骗局”。
Farmers worked harder and ate worse. Harari calls it "history's biggest fraud."

14
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:36,750
文字诞生了，但最早的文字不为写诗，只为记账。
Writing was born, not for poetry, but for keeping accounts.

15
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:41,970
村落变成城市，城市变成王国，王国变成帝国。
Villages became cities, cities became kingdoms, kingdoms became empires.

16
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:48,050
支撑帝国的，是法律、等级与王权——一种想象的秩序。
Empires rested on laws, hierarchies and kingship: an imagined order.

17
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:52,860
只要足够多的人相信，想象的秩序就坚不可摧。
As long as enough people believe in it, an imagined order is unbreakable.

18
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:57,890
而人类，也开始被自己创造的秩序束缚。
And humans began to be bound by the very order they created.

19
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:11,150
金钱，是人类最普遍、也最有效的互信系统。
Money is the most universal and most efficient system of mutual trust ever devised.

20
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:16,450
帝国，则是过去两千五百年最常见的政治形态。
Empire has been the most common political form of the past 2,500 years.

21
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:21,820
人类不断突破自己的边界，驶向地图上的空白。
Humans kept pushing past their limits, sailing toward the blank spaces on the map.

22
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:30,260
大约五百年前，科学革命始于一个伟大的发现——承认我们的无知。
About 500 years ago, the Scientific Revolution began with a great discovery: admitting our ignorance.

23
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:33,910
从相信神明，到探索宇宙。
From believing in gods to exploring the universe.

24
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:39,710
科学、帝国与资本结盟，信用让人们敢于投资未来。
Science, empire and capital joined forces, and credit gave people the courage to invest in the future.

25
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:44,150
工业革命的本质，是一场能量转换的革命。
At its core, the Industrial Revolution was a revolution in energy conversion.

26
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:48,890
火车时刻表，让整个国家第一次对准同一座钟。
Train timetables set an entire nation to one clock for the first time.

27
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:54,880
五百年间，人口增长约十四倍，产出增长约二百四十倍。
In 500 years, population grew about fourteen-fold, and production about 240-fold.

28
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:04,640
一九六九年，人类第一次登上月球。
In 1969, humans set foot on the Moon for the first time.

29
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:13,730
从仰望星空，到成为改变星球的力量。
From gazing at the stars to becoming a force that reshapes the planet.

30
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:19,760
我们比祖先强大千百倍，却未必比他们更快乐。
We are a thousand times more powerful than our ancestors, but not necessarily happier.

31
00:03:25,850 --> 00:03:29,060
过去七万年，我们改变了世界。
Over the past 70,000 years, we have changed the world.

32
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:34,810
但未来，我们是否还能理解自己？
But in the future, will we still understand ourselves?

33
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:43,750
当人工智能、基因技术和宇宙探索改变生命本身……
As AI, genetic engineering and space exploration transform life itself...

34
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:49,810
四十亿年来第一次，智能设计正在取代自然选择。
For the first time in four billion years, intelligent design is replacing natural selection.

35
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:56,640
我们正获得近乎神的力量，却仍不清楚自己想要什么。
We are gaining almost godlike powers, yet we still don't know what we want.

36
00:03:58,850 --> 00:04:03,130
我们甚至开始挑战最古老的敌人——死亡。
We have even begun to challenge our oldest enemy: death.

37
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:10,270
真正的问题不是我们想成为什么，而是——我们想要“想要”什么？
The real question is not what we want to become, but what we want to want.

38
00:04:16,450 --> 00:04:19,990
下一章人类历史，将由谁书写？
Who will write the next chapter of human history?

39
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:32,400
我们从哪里来？
Where do we come from?

40
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:38,400
我们将走向哪里？
Where are we going?

